<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan 28- and 91-day T-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>Moldovan 28- and 91-day T-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills fell to 26.60 percent on an annual basis from 30.69 percent at the previous auction on September 24, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>91-day T-bills yielded 29.26 percent annual after 30.19.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				     Oct 1		   Sept 24</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 3.00 million lei    7.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Nominal value		1,000 lei	     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	     6.17 million	  2.59 million</p>
<p>    Sold at nominal	    3.00 million	  2.59 million</p>
<p>    Yield			  26.60 pct	     30.69 pct</p>
<p>    Price			  98.0 pct		97.7 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids		97.6-98.1 pct	 97.7-98.3 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		     Oct 31, 1996	  Oct 24, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 91-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				     Oct 1		   Sept 24</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 10.00 million lei   11.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Nominal value		1,000 lei	     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	     13.64 million	 14.32 million</p>
<p>    Sold at nominal	    10.00 million	 11.00 million</p>
<p>    Yield			  29.26 pct	     30.19 pct</p>
<p>    Price			  93.2 pct		93.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids		90.9-94.1 pct	 92.0-94.0 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		     Jan 2, 1996	   Dec 26, 1996</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
